  "narrative": "The four feature_037 signature-median subgroup tests (H48, H49, H50, H51) are highly consistent with the accepted, independently validated feature_037 association. On the registered negative direction, signed estimates are approximately +0.864, +0.779, +0.894, and +0.757, with all lower 95% bounds above +0.66 and well above the 0.15-unit threshold. I accept these as dataset-specific subgroup consistency checks and close them; they do not imply causality or external generalizability. The small differences between high and low feature_038 strata and between high and low feature_018 strata do not, by themselves, justify a credible signature interaction claim. The most informative secondary result is H24: feature_031 has a signed estimate of about +0.107, with a 95% interval of +0.035 to +0.178. This suggests a small association in the claimed direction, but the point estimate is below the 0.15-unit scientific threshold and the interval spans the threshold. Given the many screened predictors, I do not accept H24 as a meaningful secondary predictor and defer rather than validate it. The remaining new screens are not supported: feature_014, feature_006, feature_007, feature_015, feature_024, and feature_058 all have small estimates and intervals centered near zero. In particular, testing feature_007, feature_015, feature_024, and feature_058 within feature_037=0 gives no evidence that these markers were merely diluted or masked by the dominant feature_037 signal. The feature_006 estimate is opposite the registered direction but small and not meaningful, so no reversed claim is warranted. The feature_059 level_001 versus level_003 contrast is also below the threshold with an interval spanning zero. I therefore close these nonmeaningful comparisons and defer no immediate validation, reserving validation for a clearer secondary discovery or a more credible heterogeneity signal.",
  "research_notes": "Updated status: The dominant feature_037 association remains accepted and validated, with new median feature_038 and feature_018 subgroup tests adding broad consistency. H48-H51 are accepted/closed as consistency checks, not separate actionable claims. No validation requested now: no clear secondary predictor exceeds the 0.15 threshold. H24 (feature_031) is the only borderline candidate: signed effect +0.107, CI +0.035 to +0.178. It is small and below threshold, so it is unresolved/deferred; possible follow-up would require a focused conditional test or stronger independent support, but multiplicity argues against immediate validation. All new conditional marker tests within feature_037=0 are null, so those markers are not plausibly secondary effects obscured by feature_037. feature_014, feature_006, and feature_059 are closed nulls. Next broad search should revive deferred binary screens (H42-H47, H55-H57, H59) and possibly feature_036 feature_037 median checks (H52-H53) if needed, while avoiding repeated feature_037 main effects or accepted subgroup consistency tests. Continue to interpret all findings as dataset-specific associations unless independently validated, and avoid causal or generalizable mechanistic language."
}

