  "narrative": "The newly released validation for H31 strongly supports the feature_037 subgroup association within the feature_058=1 stratum. On the registered negative direction, the discovery effect was approximately +0.818 (95% interval +0.719 to +0.918), and the validation effect was approximately +0.851 (validation-adjusted interval +0.726 to +0.975). Interpreted on the raw outcome scale, feature_037=1 versus feature_037=0 is associated with a lower composite dependency score by roughly 0.82 to 0.85 units in this subgroup; lower values mean stronger dependency. The validation lower bound remains far above the 0.15-unit scientific threshold. I therefore accept and close H31 as a dataset-specific consistency check for the dominant feature_037 association. This does not support feature_058 as a predictor and further weakens any attempt to build a biologically interpretable feature_058 interaction story.\n\nThe current scientific picture is that feature_037 is the dominant measured association with outcome_001 in this dataset. The overall association is accepted and independently validated (H13): feature_037=1 is associated with stronger composite dependency by about 0.78 to 0.83 composite dependency-score units. Subgroup checks show broad internal consistency: the effect remains large across median splits of feature_038 and feature_018, both feature_024 levels, median log_pfs strata, both feature_058 levels, and now an independently validated feature_058=1 subgroup. These subgroup findings are dataset-specific and do not establish causality or external generalizability.\n\nNegative findings are also informative. The named binary research markers feature_007 and feature_015 have null overall main effects. feature_058 is null overall and not meaningful within median feature_038 strata. The earlier tail-based feature_058/feature_038 interaction H22 is closed as not robust. feature_024, feature_053, feature_041, feature_014, feature_006, and the tested feature_059 contrast are not supported. Conditional tests within feature_037=0 show that feature_007, feature_015, feature_024, and feature_058 were not plausibly diluted or masked by the dominant feature_037 association. Invalid exact-value tests for continuous standardized signatures (H4-H6) should not be interpreted as biological nulls.\n\nThe main unresolved lead is feature_031. Its overall registered negative-direction effect is +0.107 (interval +0.035 to +0.178), i.e., a raw effect of roughly -0.11 units. This is statistically suggestive but scientifically borderline because the point estimate is below the 0.15 threshold and the interval crosses it. Given the number of screened predictors, I do not accept H24 yet. Instead, I registered two refinements that ask whether the feature_031 association persists or changes magnitude within feature_037=0 and feature_037=1. This distinguishes a possible genuine small secondary effect from noise or dilution by the dominant feature_037 stratum. If a conditional estimate exceeds the 0.15 threshold in the same raw direction, I will consider independent validation. If estimates remain below threshold or become inconsistent, I will reject or close the feature_031 lead.\n\nFor broader exploration, I activated H52 and H53 to complete feature_037 consistency across feature_036 median strata, and activated six additional untested binary predictors: feature_003, feature_060, feature_010, feature_048, feature_023, and feature_002, plus feature_011 and feature_021. This yields a next batch of 12 informative comparisons: two feature_031 refinements, two feature_036 median feature_037 consistency tests, and eight binary predictor screens. The overall interpretation remains noncausal and dataset-specific; independent validation supports reproducibility within the study, not mechanism or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current supported association: feature_037=1 vs 0 is accepted and independently validated for outcome_001, with raw lower outcome/stronger dependency by about -0.78 to -0.83 overall. H13 accepted/closed. H31 now accept/closed with validation R38, confirming feature_037 effect within feature_058=1. Additional feature_037 subgroup consistency tests accepted/closed: H27-H32, H48-H51. Invalid exact-value continuous tests H4-H6 remain unresolved/closed and should not be interpreted.\n\nBorderline lead: H24 feature_031 signed effect +0.107, CI +0.035 to +0.178; below threshold, unresolved/deferred. New parent-linked refinements test feature_031 within feature_037=0 and feature_037=1. If either conditional estimate is >0.15 in raw negative direction, request validation in next appraise; if not, close feature_031 as subthreshold/inconsistent.\n\nActive next batch likely includes new feature_031 conditional claims plus H42-H47, H52-H53, H55-H56. Deferred: H57, H59, H14-H21, H25-H26, H33-H34, and other untested categorical/continuous screens. Continue to avoid repeated feature_037 main effect and accepted subgroup consistency checks. Future scientific focus should remain: (1) confirm feature_037 robustness only where a new stratum adds information, (2) evaluate feature_031, (3) broad binary/categorical screen for any secondary predictor exceeding threshold, (4) validate only a clear new predictor or strong interaction, not every subgroup check. All findings remain dataset-specific associations unless externally validated."
